J Respir Crit Care Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>174</volume><fpage>538</fpage><lpage>544</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16763220</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1164/rccm.200505-693OC</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ceriello</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ihnat</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Thorpe</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The 'metabolic memory': is more than just tight glucose control necessary to prevent diabetic complications?</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>2009</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>410</fpage><lpage>415</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19066300</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1210/jc.2008-1824</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>